(527,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'South Africa beat India in two-match ODI series with De Klerk\'s storm','788787844','article','South Africa beat India in two-match ODI series with De Klerk\'s storm',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The batting will collapse in the top and middle order. Then one person will take the helm and rescue the team. This year\'s Women\'s ODI World Cup is something that is regularly seen. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batter Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls to give South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat. The batting will collapse in the top and middle order.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Then one person will take the helm and rescue the team. This year\'s Women\'s ODI World Cup is something that is regularly seen. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batter Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India got its first taste of defeat. The top and middle order will collapse in batting. Then one person will take the lead and rescue the team. This is something that this Women\'s ODI World Cup is seeing regularly.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batter Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India got its first taste of defeat. The top and middle order will collapse in batting. Then one person will take the lead and rescue the team. This is something that this Women\'s ODI World Cup is seeing regularly. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batsman Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat. The top and middle order will collapse. Then one person will take the lead and rescue the team. This is something that is regularly seen in this year\'s Women\'s ODI World Cup. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batsman Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat. The top and middle order will collapse. Then one person will take the lead and rescue the team. This Women\'s ODI World Cup is seeing something like this regularly. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batsman Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat. The batting will collapse in the top and middle order. Then someone will take the reins and rescue the team. This Women\'s ODI World Cup is seeing something like this regularly. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batsman Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls and gave South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat.</span></div>','1760082336TMJXS5Ip.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,78,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',27,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:15','2026-03-07 01:49:15','South Africa beat India in two-match ODI series with De Klerk\'s storm','The batting will collapse in the top and middle order. Then one person will take the helm and rescue the team. This year\'s Women\'s ODI World Cup is something that is regularly seen. In the last India-South Africa match on Thursday, such a picture was seen in both innings. In that match in Visakhapatnam, India\'s number eight batter Richa Ghosh\'s 94 surpassed South Africa\'s number eight Nadine de Klerk\'s 84. This all-rounder played an unbeaten innings of 84 runs off 54 balls to give South Africa a 3-wicket victory. India has tasted its first defeat. The batting will collapse in the top and middle order.'),
(528,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kabrera took responsibility for the defeat on his own shoulders.','4458888','article','Kabrera took responsibility for the defeat on his own shoulders.',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Once again, the picture of disappointment at the end of that loss! However, such a loss is burning Bangladesh a little too much. Leading by a goal at the beginning, then falling behind by 3-1. Returning to the tie with 2 goals, the equalizing goal again in the ninth minute of added time. Bangladesh could have ended the match with at least one point. But the hosts lost to a young man of French origin. Just before the referee\'s final whistle, in the added time, Hong Kong\'s 23-year-old forward Raphael Marquis threw sand into Bangladesh\'s hopes of a point.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">After conceding a goal at the last minute in a tense match and losing 4-3, Bangladesh coach Javier Cabrera took the responsibility on his shoulders. At the press conference after the match, Cabrera said, \"I take all the responsibility, the whole team takes it. The biggest responsibility is mine.\" Once again, the picture of disappointment at the end of that loss! However, such a loss is burning Bangladesh a little too much. Leading by a goal at the beginning, then falling behind by 3-1. 2 goals to equalize again, the equalizing goal was again in the ninth minute of added time. Bangladesh could have ended the match with at least one point. But the hosts lost to a young man of French origin. Just before the referee\'s final whistle, in the added time, 23-year-old forward Rafael Marquis of Hong Kong threw sand into the dust of Bangladesh\'s hopes of a point.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">After conceding a goal at the last minute of a tense match and losing 4-3, Bangladesh coach Javier Cabrera took the responsibility on his shoulders. At the press conference after the match, Cabrera said, \"I take all the responsibility, the whole team takes it. The most responsibility is mine.\" Once again, the picture of disappointment at the end of that loss! However, such a loss is burning Bangladesh a little too much. Leading by scoring a goal at the beginning, then falling behind by 3-1. 2 goals to equalize again, the equalizing goal was again in the ninth minute of added time. Bangladesh could have ended the match with at least one point. But the hosts lost to a young Frenchman. Just before the referee\'s final whistle, in added time, Hong Kong\'s 23-year-old forward Raphael Marquis dashed Bangladesh\'s hopes of a point.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh coach Javier Cabrera took the blame for the 4-3 defeat in a tense match after conceding a last-minute goal. Cabrera said at the post-match press conference, \"I take all the responsibility, the whole team takes it too. The biggest responsibility lies with me.\"</span></div>','1760082449EbPcz0FR.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,78,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',20,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:14','2026-03-07 01:49:14','Kabrera took responsibility for the defeat on his own shoulders.','Once again, the picture of disappointment at the end of that loss! However, such a loss is burning Bangladesh a little too much. Leading by a goal at the beginning, then falling behind by 3-1. Returning to the tie with 2 goals, the equalizing goal again in the ninth minute of added time. Bangladesh could have ended the match with at least one point. But the hosts lost to a young man of French origin. Just before the referee\'s final whistle, in the added time, Hong Kong\'s 23-year-old forward Raphael Marquis threw sand into Bangladesh\'s hopes of a point.'),
(529,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I never thought I would come back like this, says Shamit Som','45455445884','article','I never thought I would come back like this, says Shamit Som',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh is still winless in the 2027 Asian Cup qualifiers. After starting with a draw against India, the team lost 2-1 against Singapore. With this, Bangladesh lost two consecutive matches in the qualifiers.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh also conceded goals due to their own mistakes against Singapore. This was a continuation of yesterday. Shamit himself says that goals cannot be given so easily. He said, \'We have conceded goals like this against Singapore. We have to learn from these. We cannot give such easy goals. We cannot win the game by giving such easy goals. We have to learn nothing. Everyone knows what to do, we will review the videos. The coach will teach us how to defend better in the backline and midfield. At the end of the day, it is everyone\'s responsibility. This is football. There will be ups and downs. They had their chances, we had ours. This is international football, it is clear that it is different from club football.\' Bangladesh is still winless in the 2027 Asian Cup qualifiers. After starting with a draw against India, the team lost 2-1 against Singapore. Bangladesh lost two consecutive matches in the qualifiers.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh also conceded goals against Singapore due to their own mistakes. This was a continuation of yesterday. Shamit himself says that goals cannot be conceded so easily. He said, \'We conceded goals like this against Singapore. We have to learn from these. We cannot give such easy goals. We cannot win the game by giving such easy goals. We have to learn, there is nothing we can do. Everyone knows what to do, we will review the videos. The coach will teach us how to defend better in the backline and midfield. At the end of the day, it is everyone\'s responsibility. This is football. There will be ups and downs. They had their chances, we had ours. This is international football, it is clear that it is different from club football.\'</span></div>','17600825526TQbdBnB.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,78,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',18,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:13','2026-03-07 01:49:13','I never thought I would come back like this, says Shamit Som','Bangladesh is still winless in the 2027 Asian Cup qualifiers. After starting with a draw against India, the team lost 2-1 against Singapore. With this, Bangladesh lost two consecutive matches in the qualifiers.\r\nBangladesh is still winless in the 2027 Asian Cup qualifiers. After starting with a draw against India, the team lost 2-1 against Singapore. With this, Bangladesh lost two consecutive matches in the qualifiers.'),
(530,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sourav on Rohit\'s captaincy being taken away, \'It happened to me too, it happened to Dravid too\'','78755778758','article','Sourav on Rohit\'s captaincy being taken away, \'It happened to me too, it happened to Dravid too\'',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Former India captain Sourav Ganguly does not think it was wrong to replace Rohit Sharma with Shubman Gill as the ODI captain. Rohit will be 40 in the 2027 ODI World Cup.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Ganguly believes that this is the main reason for removing Rohit. The former BCCI president also claimed that he and Rahul Dravid have also gone through the same experience.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Talking to reporters in Kolkata on Friday, Sourav said, \"I do not know whether Rohit has been removed or something else. But it seems that it was discussed between the two parties. Because Rohit is an extraordinary captain. In the last two years, Rohit has won the T20 World Cup and the Champions Trophy. So there is no question about Rohit\'s performance. What came to the mind of the selectors is that Rohit will be 40 in two years during the World Cup.\"</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Former India captain Sourav Ganguly does not think it was wrong to replace Rohit Sharma with Shubman Gill as the ODI captain. Rohit will be 40 in the 2027 ODI World Cup.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Ganguly believes this is the main reason for removing Rohit. The former BCCI president also claimed that he and Rahul Dravid have also gone through the same experience.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Talking to reporters in Kolkata on Friday, Sourav said, \"I don\'t know if Rohit has been removed or something else. But it seems that it was discussed between the two parties. Because Rohit is an extraordinary captain. In the last two years, Rohit has won the T20 World Cup and the Champions Trophy. So there is no question about Rohit\'s performance. What has come to the mind of the selectors is that Rohit will be 40 in the World Cup in two years.\"</span></div>','17600826269CSY21wz.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,78,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',16,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:12','2026-03-07 01:49:12','Sourav on Rohit\'s captaincy being taken away, \'It happened to me too, it happened to Dravid too\'','Talking to reporters in Kolkata on Friday, Sourav said, \"I do not know whether Rohit has been removed or something else. But it seems that it was discussed between the two parties. Because Rohit is an extraordinary captain. In the last two years, Rohit has won the T20 World Cup and the Champions Trophy. So there is no question about Rohit\'s performance. What came to the mind of the selectors is that Rohit will be 40 in two years during the World Cup.\"'),
(531,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'That day I realized that the world is not safe for girls...','45454554','article','That day I realized that the world is not safe for girls...',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">‘Rekha means a mystery, a pain, and a woman—who has risen from her own ashes.’ Indian writer and journalist Yasir Osman described Rekha this way in his biography ‘Rekha: The Untold Story’. He wrote about the life of this Bollywood star, built on beauty, gossip, mystery, and resistance. That book highlights an unknown Rekha—who was in the light and remained bright in the darkness. According to many film critics including Yasir Osman, there are many stars in Bollywood whose lives are more dramatic than movies. But Rekha seems to be above everything.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Rekha has returned to Facebook and Instagram since last night. It was as if a shower of wishes had fallen on social media. Rekha, even after seventy, seems to have returned to the net world.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Of course, it would be wrong to say ‘returned’. When was Rekha not there? Rekha has been around for years—she is in the news, she is a bright star on a starry evening. Rekha herself is always new. Writing ‘evergreen’ next to her name is not an exaggeration. She captivates the hearts of teenagers, young adults, adults, and even the elderly. ‘Rekha means a mystery, a pain, and a woman—who has risen from her own ashes.’ Indian writer and journalist Yasir Osman describes Rekha this way in his biography ‘Rekha: The Untold Story.’ He wrote about the life of this Bollywood star, built on beauty, eloquence, mystery, and resistance. That book highlights an unknown Rekha—who was in the light and remained bright in the dark. According to many film critics, including Yasir Osman, there are many stars in Bollywood whose lives are more dramatic than movies. But Rekha seems to be above everything.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Rekha has returned to Facebook and Instagram since last night. It was as if a shower of greetings had poured down on social media. Even after seventy, Rekha has returned to the internet world.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Of course, it would be wrong to say \'returned\'. When was Rekha not there? Rekha has been around for years—she is in the news, she is a bright star on a starry evening. Rekha herself is always new. It is not an exaggeration to write \'evergreen\' next to her name. The one who captivates the hearts of teenagers, young people, young adults, and even the elderly. \'Rekha means a mystery, a pain, and a woman—who has risen from her own ashes.\' Indian writer and journalist Yasir Osman described Rekha this way in his biography \'Rekha: The Untold Story\'. He wrote about the life of this Bollywood star built on beauty, gossip, mystery, and resistance. That book has highlighted an unknown Rekha—who was in the light and remained bright in the darkness. According to many film critics including Yasir Osman, there are many stars in Bollywood whose lives are more dramatic than movies. But Rekha seems to be above everything.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Rekha has returned to Facebook and Instagram since last night. It was as if a shower of greetings had fallen on social media. Even after seventy, Rekha has returned to the net world.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Of course, it would be wrong to say ‘returned’. When was Rekha not there? Rekha has been there for years—she is in the stories, she is there as a bright star on a starry evening. Rekha herself seems to be always new. Writing ‘evergreen’ next to her name is not an exaggeration. The one who captivates the hearts of teenagers, young people, young adults, adults, and even the elderly.</span></div>','1760082768A3GlYPiP.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,79,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',26,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:20','2026-03-07 01:49:20','That day I realized that the world is not safe for girls...','‘Rekha means a mystery, a pain, and a woman—who has risen from her own ashes.’ Indian writer and journalist Yasir Osman described Rekha this way in his biography ‘Rekha: The Untold Story’. He wrote about the life of this Bollywood star, built on beauty, gossip, mystery, and resistance. That book highlights an unknown Rekha—who was in the light and remained bright in the darkness. According to many film critics including Yasir Osman, there are many stars in Bollywood whose lives are more dramatic than movies. But Rekha seems to be above everything.'),
(532,1,15,NULL,NULL,'Salman\'s co-star in \'Tiger 3\' Barinder passes away','545454545454','article','Salman\'s co-star in \'Tiger 3\' Barinder passes away',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Professional bodybuilder and actor Barinder Singh Ghuman has passed away. He died of a heart attack on Thursday. Barinder was 41 years old. According to NDTV, Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. While undergoing treatment there, he died of a heart attack in the evening. Barinder\'s nephew Amanjot Singh Ghuman told reporters in Jalandhar, \"He suddenly had a heart attack in the evening in the hospital.\" Professional bodybuilder and actor Barinder Singh Ghuman has passed away. He died of a heart attack on Thursday. Barinder was 41 years old. According to NDTV, Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. He died of a heart attack in the evening while undergoing treatment there.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Barinder\'s nephew Amanjot Singh Ghuman told reporters in Jalandhar, \"He suddenly had a heart attack in the evening in the hospital.\" Professional bodybuilder and actor Barinder Singh Ghuman has died. He died of a heart attack on Thursday. Barinder was 41 years old. NDTV News</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. He died of a heart attack in the evening while undergoing treatment there.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Barinder\'s nephew Amanjot Singh Ghuman told reporters in Jalandhar, \"He suddenly had a heart attack in the evening in the hospital.\" Professional bodybuilder and actor Barinder Singh Ghuman died. He died of a heart attack on Thursday. Barinder was 41 years old. According to NDTV, Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. He died of a heart attack in the evening while undergoing treatment there. Barinder\'s nephew Amanjot Singh Ghuman told reporters in Jalandhar, \"He suddenly had a heart attack in the evening in the hospital.\"</span></div>','1760083105aXnqNira.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,79,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',20,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 09:08:20','2026-03-12 03:08:20','Salman\'s co-star in \'Tiger 3\' Barinder passes away','Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. He died of a heart attack in the evening while undergoing treatment there.Barinder\'s manager Jadwinder Singh said that he was admitted to a private hospital in Amritsar, Punjab, for treatment after feeling pain in his shoulder yesterday evening. He died of a heart attack in the evening while undergoing treatment there.'),
(533,1,15,NULL,NULL,'\'I didn\'t want to miss the opportunity to work with Shakib Khan\'','5455454','article',NULL,0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Earlier, Tanjin Tisha was supposed to act opposite Shakib Khan in the movie \'Premik\'. That film was supposed to be directed by Raihan Rafi, but the shooting has not started. Finally, the much-awaited pair is going to be realized through \'Soldier\'.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Tanjin Tisha needed to get a visa from that country to act in an Indian film. But even as the shooting time approached, she did not get a visa. After that, she did not try again. Explaining the reason, Tisha said, \'I am a Bangladeshi girl. Bangladesh comes first for me. That is why \"Soldier\" is my first choice.\' Earlier, Tanjin Tisha was supposed to act opposite Shakib Khan in the movie \'Premik\'. That film was supposed to be directed by Raihan Rafi, but the shooting has not started. Finally, the much-awaited pair is going to be realized through \'Soldier\'.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Tanjin Tisha needed to get a visa from that country to act in an Indian film. But even as the shooting time approached, she did not get a visa. After that, she did not try again. Explaining the reason, Tisha said, \"I am a Bangladeshi girl. Bangladesh comes first to me. So \"Soldier\" is my first choice.\" Earlier, Tanjin Tisha was supposed to act opposite Shakib Khan in the movie \"Premik.\" That movie was supposed to be directed by Raihan Rafi, but the shooting never started. Finally, the much-awaited pair is going to be realized through \"Soldier.\"</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Tanjin Tisha needed to get a visa from that country to act in an Indian movie. But even as the shooting time approached, she did not get a visa. After that, she did not try anymore. Explaining the reason, Tisha said, \"I am a Bangladeshi girl. Bangladesh comes first to me. So \"Soldier\" is my first choice.\" Earlier, Tanjin Tisha was supposed to act opposite Shakib Khan in the movie \"Premik.\" That movie was supposed to be directed by Raihan Rafi, but the shooting never started. Finally, the much-awaited pair is going to be realized through \"Soldier.\"</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Tanjin Tisha needed to get a visa from that country to act in an Indian film. But even as the shooting time approached, she could not get a visa. After that, she did not try again. Explaining the reason, Tisha said, \"I am a Bangladeshi girl. Bangladesh comes first for me. That is why \"Soldier\" is my first choice.\"</span></div>','1760083212nJy2xxnz.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,79,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',20,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 08:38:58','2026-03-12 02:38:58','\'I didn\'t want to miss the opportunity to work with Shakib Khan\'','Earlier, Tanjin Tisha was supposed to act opposite Shakib Khan in the movie \'Premik\'. That film was supposed to be directed by Raihan Rafi, but the shooting has not started. Finally, the much-awaited pair is going to be realized through \'Soldier\'.'),
(534,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Threat to blow up Vijay\'s house with a bomb','544565456','article','Threat to blow up Vijay\'s house with a bomb',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Vijay is now in the news in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather politician Vijay. He is in the news in various incidents before the start of his political innings in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. In this incident, even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the house of the southern star yesterday, Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail. According to The Hindu, Vijay is now in the news in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather politician Vijay. He is in the news in various incidents before the start of his political innings in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. In this incident, even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the house of the southern star yesterday, Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail. According to The Hindu, Vijay is now in the news in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather politician Vijay. Rather, politician Vijay. He was in the news for various incidents before his political innings began in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. In this incident, even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the house of the southern star yesterday, Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail. According to The Hindu, Vijay is now the talk of the town in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather, politician Vijay. He was in the news for various incidents before his political innings began in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. In this incident, even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the house of the southern star yesterday, Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail. According to The Hindu, Vijay is now the talk of the town in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather, politician Vijay. He is in the news for various incidents before his political innings begins in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. Even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone in this incident. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the southern star\'s house on Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail. According to The Hindu</span>','17600833042XuOXAlg.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,79,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',23,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 01:47:18','2026-03-11 19:47:18','Threat to blow up Vijay\'s house with a bomb','Vijay is now in the news in South India. However, actor Thalapathy Vijay is not; rather politician Vijay. He is in the news in various incidents before the start of his political innings in the 26th assembly elections. A few days ago, many people were killed in a stampede at his public meeting. In this incident, even the opposition camp did not leave the southern superstar alone. In such an atmosphere, there was a bomb scare at the house of the southern star yesterday, Thursday. Thalapathy Vijay received a threat to blow up his house via e-mail.'),
(535,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Our graduates have proven their skills at the national and international levels.','54546456654654','article','Our graduates have proven their skills at the national and international levels.',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">My journey with the Youth Engagement and Support, or YES Club in short, began in my first year. I have been with the club for more than three and a half years. Although it seemed like just a club in the beginning, this organization has become like my family with time.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Not only YES, but all the other clubs in UAP have a different culture. We learn to take responsibility and lead through the club\'s work. Starting from financial sponsorship to ancillary support, the university authorities are always by our side.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Our YES Club is basically a \'student wing\' of Transparency International Bangladesh (TIB). Therefore, many of our activities are conducted in collaboration with TIB, which makes our work more meaningful.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In the last few years, we have done various things including seminars, workshops, campaigns, awareness programs, and anti-corruption plays. For example, we did a play at the club fair last semester, the topic was market syndicates.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">My journey with the Youth Engagement and Support, or YES Club in short, began in my first year. I have been with the club for more than three and a half years. Although it seemed like just a club at the beginning, this organization has become like my family with time.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Not only YES, but all the other clubs in UAP have a different culture. We learn to take responsibility and lead through the club\'s work. Starting from financial sponsorship to ancillary support, the university authorities are always by our side.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Our YES Club is basically a \'student wing\' of Transparency International Bangladesh (TIB). Therefore, many of our activities are carried out in collaboration with TIB, which makes our work more meaningful.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In the last few years, we have done various things including seminars, workshops, campaigns, awareness programs, anti-corruption plays. For example, we did a play at the club fair last semester, the topic was market syndicates.</span></div>','1760083425MhUQYqhs.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,77,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',20,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:11','2026-03-07 01:49:11','Our graduates have proven their skills at the national and international levels.','My journey with the Youth Engagement and Support, or YES Club in short, began in my first year. I have been with the club for more than three and a half years. Although it seemed like just a club in the beginning, this organization has become like my family with time.'),
