 and Grade: 16,000-38,640/- (Grade-10)</span></div>','1760084373hWQF2eW1.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',17,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:49:39','2026-03-07 01:49:39','Job opportunities in various grades including 9th in Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park','Bangladesh Hi-Tech Park has published a recruitment notice for four posts from grades 9 to 16. The recruitment notice was published yesterday, Wednesday.\r\nBangladesh Hi-Tech Park has published a recruitment notice for four posts from grades 9 to 16. The recruitment notice was published yesterday, Wednesday.'),
(545,1,15,NULL,NULL,'49th BCS (Special) exam today, candidates will have to follow the instructions','565675767576','article','49th BCS (Special) exam today, candidates will have to follow the instructions',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The 49th BCS (Special) MCQ type written exam will be held today, Friday (October 10). Before this, the exam seating arrangement, schedule and various instructions for students have been published on the Bangladesh Public Service Commission website.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The 49th BCS (Special) 2025 is a special BCS of education. 683 posts of general education cadre will be recruited in this BCS. A total of more than 3 lakh 12 thousand candidates have applied for the 683 posts of the 49th BCS (Special). The number of applicants against each post is more than 456.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Schedule and Center</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It will be held on October 10 from 10 am to 12 noon in 184 centers in Dhaka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">What the candidates should do</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1. Candidates must enter the examination hall by 9:30 am. No candidate will be able to enter the hall after 9:30 am.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">2. Answer sheets will be distributed among the candidates. There will be four sets of answer sheets, namely set # 1, 2, 3 and 4.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3. After the distribution of the question papers, no candidate will be allowed to leave the examination room until the examination is over (12 noon).</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4. It is completely prohibited to bring books, all types of watches, mobile phones, calculators, all types of electronic devices, bank cards or credit card-like devices, jewelry and bags into the examination center.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">5. During the examination, candidates should not wear any covering on their ears, their ears should be kept open. If any type of hearing aid is required, the approval of the commission along with a specialist doctor\'s recommendation letter must be obtained.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">6. No application by candidates to change the examination hall will be considered.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">7. Arrangements have been made by the commission to appoint dictation scribes in response to the application of disabled candidates. No one other than the dictation scribes nominated by the commission can participate in the examination as dictation scribes. For visually impaired candidates, 10 minutes of extra time will be given for every hour of the test in the case of dictation, and five minutes of extra time will be given for every hour of the test in the case of other disabilities.</span></div></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The 49th BCS (Special) 2025 is a special BCS of education. 683 posts of general education cadre will be recruited in this BCS. A total of more than 3 lakh 12 thousand candidates have applied for the 683 posts of the 49th BCS (Special). The number of applicants against each post is more than 456.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Schedule and Center</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It will be held on October 10 from 10 am to 12 noon in 184 centers in Dhaka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">What the candidates should do</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1. Candidates must enter the examination hall by 9:30 am. No candidate will be able to enter the hall after 9:30 am.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">2. Answer sheets will be distributed among the candidates. There will be four sets of answer sheets, namely set # 1, 2, 3 and 4.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3. After the distribution of the question papers, no candidate will be allowed to leave the examination room until the examination is over (12 noon).</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4. It is completely prohibited to bring books, all types of watches, mobile phones, calculators, all types of electronic devices, bank cards or credit card-like devices, jewelry and bags into the examination center.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">5. During the examination, candidates should not wear any covering on their ears, their ears should be kept open. If any type of hearing aid is required, the approval of the commission along with a specialist doctor\'s recommendation letter must be obtained.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">6. No application by candidates to change the examination hall will be considered.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">7. Arrangements have been made by the commission to appoint dictation scribes in response to the application of disabled candidates. No one other than the dictation scribes nominated by the commission can participate in the examination as dictation scribes. For visually impaired candidates, 10 minutes of extra time will be given for every hour of the test in the case of dictation, and five minutes of extra time will be given for every hour of the test in the case of other disabilities.</span></div>','1760084470oIHWb8Nn.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',32,0,NULL,'2026-03-11 21:52:30','2026-03-11 15:52:30','49th BCS (Special) exam today, candidates will have to follow the instructions','The 49th BCS (Special) MCQ type written exam will be held today, Friday (October 10). Before this, the exam seating arrangement, schedule and various instructions for students have been published on the Bangladesh Public Service Commission website.The 49th BCS (Special) MCQ type written exam will be held today, Friday (October 10). Before this, the exam seating arrangement, schedule and various instructions for students have been published on the Bangladesh Public Service Commission website.'),
(546,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'PSC written exam date and schedule announced, total number of candidates 1398','534435454354','article','PSC written exam date and schedule announced, total number of candidates 1398',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The date and schedule of the written examination for the post of ‘Personal Officer’ (10th Grade) organized by the Bangladesh Public Service Commission has been published. A total of 1398 candidates have been selected.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Exam details:</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Post Name: Personal Officer (10th Grade)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Exam Type: Written Examination</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Exam Date: 23 October 2025, Thursday</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Time: 2:30 PM to 4:00 PM</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Exam Center:</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1. Government Mohammadpur Model School and College, College Gate, Mohammadpur, Dhaka</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">2. 71 Auditorium, Bangladesh Public Service Commission Bhaban, Agargaon, Sher-e-Bangla Nagar, Dhaka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Important Instructions Regarding the Exam—</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Candidates must take their own admit card to participate in the exam. If the admit card is lost or damaged, it can be downloaded and collected from the Bangladesh Public Service Commission website.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You must arrive at the center at least 15 minutes before the scheduled time of the exam. No candidate will be allowed to enter after 15 minutes of the start of the exam.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The registration number must be written and filled in correctly on the answer sheet. No cutting or fluid of any kind can be used, otherwise the candidature will be cancelled.</span></div>','1760084551oiGEp7rA.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',32,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 15:18:39','2026-03-12 09:18:39','PSC written exam date and schedule announced, total number of candidates 1398','The date and schedule of the written examination for the post of ‘Personal Officer’ (10th Grade) organized by the Bangladesh Public Service Commission has been published. A total of 1398 candidates have been selected.The date and schedule of the written examination for the post of ‘Personal Officer’ (10th Grade) organized by the Bangladesh Public Service Commission has been published. A total of 1398 candidates have been selected.'),
(547,1,11,NULL,NULL,'Jobs in Patuakhali under the Ministry of Local Government, Post 74','6565464654','article','Jobs in Patuakhali under the Ministry of Local Government, Post 74',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">A notification has been published for the recruitment of manpower for the post of ‘Accounting Assistant cum-Computer Operator’ in the Union Parishads of Patuakhali district under the Local Government Division of the Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives. A total of 74 vacant posts will be filled in this notification.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Name and number of posts details—</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Name of post: Accounting Assistant cum-Computer Operator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of posts: 74</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary scale: 9300–22490/- Taka (75 percent of salary and allowance is paid by the government and 25 percent by the Union Parishad.)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Grade: 16 (as per National Pay Scale-2015)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational qualification: Higher Secondary Certificate in Commerce with minimum second division or equivalent GPA from a recognized board or equivalent examination passed. Computer trained and should have a minimum speed of 20 words per minute in Bengali and English in computer typing.</span></div>','1760085184yeTJigsk.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',25,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 07:18:07','2026-03-12 01:18:07','Jobs in Patuakhali under the Ministry of Local Government, Post 74','A notification has been published for the recruitment of manpower for the post of ‘Accounting Assistant cum-Computer Operator’ in the Union Parishads of Patuakhali district under the Local Government Division of the Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives. A total of 74 vacant posts will be filled in this notification.'),
(548,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is it possible to build a career in communications in the future?','3543545','article','Is it possible to build a career in communications in the future?',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Lately, many people are asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, as the budget in the development sector is decreasing?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience on whether it is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You have to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Lately, many people are asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, as the budget in the development sector is decreasing?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience on whether it is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You have to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is not what you are doing now; it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You have to know how to predict the impact of these in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications are not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a ‘support role’ for the rest of your life. Recently, many people have been asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, as the budget in the development sector is decreasing?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience on whether it is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You have to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is not what you are doing now; rather, it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You have to know how to predict the impact of these in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications are not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a ‘support role’ for the rest of your life. Recently, many people have been asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, as the budget in the development sector is decreasing?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience on whether it is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You need to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is no longer what you are doing; it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You need to know how to predict what the impact of these can be in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications are not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a \'support role\' for the rest of your life.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience of what is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You need to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is no longer what you are doing; it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You need to know how to predict what the impact of these can be in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications is not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a ‘support role’ for the rest of its life. Recently, many people have been asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, since the budget in the development sector is decreasing?</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This article is based on my experience on whether it is possible or impossible.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">You have to develop yourself as a strategic communicator</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">It is not what you are doing now; rather, it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You need to know how to predict the impact of these in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications is not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a ‘support role’ for the rest of its life.</span></div>','17600852928aLWj0pQ.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',25,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 08:27:22','2026-03-12 02:27:22','Is it possible to build a career in communications in the future?','It is not what you are doing now; it is important to know the answer to why you are doing it. Just taking pictures, making videos, writing press releases or stories is not enough. You have to know how to predict the impact of these in advance and show their impact in reality. If communications are not linked to the output of a program or project, it will be limited to a ‘support role’ for the rest of your life. Recently, many people have been asking, is it possible to build a career in communications in the future, as the budget in the development sector is decreasing?'),
(549,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Allegations of voice grabbing, case against owner','53325234','article','Allegations of voice grabbing, case against owner',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">A group of employees of the Dhaka-based Bengali newspaper Janakantha, who were employed by the newspaper at various times after the fall of the Awami League government on August 5 last year, have formed an editorial board of their own, declaring the editor undesirable.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In retaliation for the dismissal of some of them by the owners on Saturday, they have also filed a case against the owners at Hatirjheel Police Station in Dhaka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Janakantha editor and publisher Shamima A Khan alleged that the Janakantha Bhaban was illegally occupied by conspiring to create a mob on Saturday night. His complaint is against retired Major Afizur Rahman, Chief Operating Officer of Globe Janakantha Industrial Group, Jatiya Nagorik Party (NCP) Joint Convener and Planning Advisor of the newspaper Joynal Abedin, as well as some Islamist journalists from BNP and Jamaat (Shishir). A group of employees of the newspaper, who were appointed to the newspaper at various times after the fall of the Awami League government on August 5 last year, have declared the editor of the Dhaka-based Bengali newspaper Janakantha as undesirable and formed an editorial board of their own.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">After the owners fired some of them on Saturday, in retaliation, they declared the editor as undesirable and filed a case against the owners at Hatirjheel Police Station in Dhaka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Janakantha Editor and Publisher Shamima A Khan has alleged that the Janakantha Bhaban was illegally occupied by conspiring on Saturday night by creating a mob. His complaint is against retired Major Afizur Rahman, Chief Operating Officer of the Globe Janakantha industry group, Jatiya Nagorik Party (NCP) joint convener and the newspaper\'s planning advisor Joynal Abedin (Shishir), and several Islamist journalists from BNP and Jamaat.</span></div>','1760085370VIrGIiZd.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',28,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 22:43:53','2026-03-07 16:43:53','Allegations of voice grabbing, case against owner','A group of employees of the Dhaka-based Bengali newspaper Janakantha, who were employed by the newspaper at various times after the fall of the Awami League government on August 5 last year, have formed an editorial board of their own, declaring the editor undesirable.'),
(550,1,15,NULL,NULL,'96th BMA course in Bangladesh Army, who has the opportunity to apply','7575676','article','96th BMA course in Bangladesh Army, who has the opportunity to apply',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh Army has published a notification to join the 96th BMA (Bangladesh Military Academy) long-term course as an officer cadet. Applications can be submitted until October 18.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Age and eligibility for application—</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational qualification: Must have passed either SSC or HSC with a minimum GPA of 5 and must have passed the other with a GPA of 4.50.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Age: Minimum 16 and a half years and maximum 21 years as on January 1, 2026.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Minimum height: Male 5 feet 4 inches, Female 5 feet 2 inches.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">*Applicant must be unmarried.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary and allowances</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary and allowances will be provided as per the pay scale of the armed forces.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application process</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Apply online on the army website.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application fee must be paid through the prescribed mobile banking service.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application fee</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Total 2000 taka including application fee 1000 taka and online registration fee 1000 taka.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Age and Qualifications for Application—</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational Qualifications: Must have passed either SSC or HSC with a minimum GPA of 5 and must have passed the other with a GPA of 4.50.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Age: Minimum 16.5 years and maximum 21 years as on January 1, 2026.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Minimum height: Male 5 feet 4 inches, Female 5 feet 2 inches.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">*Applicant must be unmarried.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary and Allowance</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary and allowances will be provided as per the pay scale of the armed forces.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application Process</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Apply online on the army website.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application fee must be paid through the designated mobile banking service.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Application Fee</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Total 2000 taka including application fee 1000 taka and online registration fee 1000 taka.</span></div>','1760085441AAnnwzwh.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',123,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 11:17:19','2026-03-12 05:17:19','96th BMA course in Bangladesh Army, who has the opportunity to apply','Bangladesh Army has published a notification to join the 96th BMA (Bangladesh Military Academy) long-term course as an officer cadet. Applications can be submitted until October 18.Bangladesh Army has published a notification to join the 96th BMA (Bangladesh Military Academy) long-term course as an officer cadet. Applications can be submitted until October 18.'),
(551,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'11 banks including Sonali-Agrani-Krishi-Rupali will recruit senior officers, 1017 posts','5454545454','article','11 banks including Sonali-Agrani-Krishi-Rupali will recruit senior officers, 1017 posts',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Integrated Bank Recruitment Circular 2025 has been published under the supervision of the Bankers Selection Committee. This circular has been published for the recruitment of manpower for the post of Senior Officer (General) in 9 banks and 2 financial institutions. 1,17 people will be appointed in 9 banks and 2 financial institutions. Interested and eligible candidates can apply for these posts of Senior Officer (General).</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Job Description</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Post Name: Senior Officer (General)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of Posts: 1,017</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary Scale: 22,000–53,060 Taka. Other Benefits as per Rules</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Name of Bank and Number of Posts</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1. Sonali Bank PLC—118</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">2. Agrani Bank PLC—200</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3. Rupali Bank PLC—75</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4. Bangladesh Development Bank PLC—21</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">5. Bangladesh Krishi Bank—398</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">6. Rajshahi Krishi Unnayan Bank—6</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">7. Karmasangsthan Bank—18</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">8. Probashi Kalyan Bank—37</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">9. Rural Savings Bank 114</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">10. Bangladesh House Building Finance Corporation 15</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">11. Investment Corporation of Bangladesh 15.</span></div>','1760085996rUh0Ifr7.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',70,0,NULL,'2026-03-15 14:00:52','2026-03-15 08:00:52','11 banks including Sonali-Agrani-Krishi-Rupali will recruit senior officers, 1017 posts','The Integrated Bank Recruitment Circular 2025 has been published under the supervision of the Bankers Selection Committee. This circular has been published for the recruitment of manpower for the post of Senior Officer (General) in 9 banks and 2 financial institutions. 1,17 people will be appointed in 9 banks and 2 financial institutions. Interested and eligible candidates can apply for these posts of Senior Officer (General).\r\nJob Description'),
