(554,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Recruitment for various grades including 10th at Rice Research Institute, 49 posts','515115','article','Recruitment for various grades including 10th at Rice Research Institute, 49 posts',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladesh Rice Research Institute (BRI) has published a notification for the recruitment of manpower for 27 categories of posts under the revenue budget. This notification is published for a total of 49 posts from grades 10 to 20. Applications for these posts will start tomorrow, Tuesday, October 7. The last date for applications is October 30.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Name and description of the post</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1. Sub Assistant Engineer (Permanent)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of posts: 01</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational qualification and experience: Diploma in Civil Engineering from a recognized board or institute or organization with at least 3 years of practical work experience in related work.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary scale and grade: 16,000-38,680 taka (Grade-10)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">2. Sub-Assistant Engineer (Temporary)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of posts: 04</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational qualification and experience: Diploma in Civil Engineering from a recognized board or institute or organization with at least 3 years of practical work experience in related work.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary Scale and Grade: 16,000-38,680 Taka (Grade-10)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3. Data Analyst</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of Posts: 01</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational Qualifications and Experience: Must have a Master\'s degree in Statistics/Geography/Mathematics or equivalent from a recognized university with at least 2 years of practical work experience in data processing and computer operation.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary Scale and Grade: 16,000-38,680 Taka (Grade-10)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4. Transport Supervisor</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Number of Posts: 01</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Educational Qualifications and Experience: Must have a Diploma in Automobile Engineering from a recognized board or institute or organization with at least 3 years of practical work experience in related work.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Salary Scale and Grade: 16,000-38,680 Taka (Grade-10)</span></div>','1760086225w8qREccD.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,81,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',27,0,NULL,'2026-03-08 22:00:21','2026-03-08 16:00:21','Recruitment for various grades including 10th at Rice Research Institute, 49 posts','Bangladesh Rice Research Institute (BRI) has published a notification for the recruitment of manpower for 27 categories of posts under the revenue budget. This notification is published for a total of 49 posts from grades 10 to 20. Applications for these posts will start tomorrow, Tuesday, October 7. The last date for applications is October 30.'),
(555,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'There will be no restrictions on media in national elections: Information Advisor','46455454','article','There will be no restrictions on media in national elections: Information Advisor',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national parliamentary elections. However, journalists will have to play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The information advisor said this in his speech at a meeting on the role of the media during the elections on Sunday. The meeting was held at the DFP meeting room at the Information Building in Dhaka. Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national parliamentary elections. However, journalists will have to play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The information advisor said this in his speech at a meeting on the role of the media during the elections on Sunday. The meeting was held at the DFP meeting room at the Information Building in Dhaka. Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national elections. However, journalists will have to play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The information advisor said this in his speech at a meeting on the role of the media during the elections on Sunday. The meeting was held at the DFP meeting room at the Information Building in Dhaka. Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national elections. However, journalists will have to play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The information advisor said this in his speech at a meeting on the role of the media during the elections on Sunday. The meeting was held at the DFP meeting room at the Information Building in Dhaka. Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national elections. However, journalists must play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The information advisor said this in his speech at a view-sharing meeting on the role of the media during the elections on Sunday. The meeting was held at the DFP meeting room at the Information Building in Dhaka.</span></div>','1760086337u2utLthD.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,80,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',12,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 09:02:28','2026-03-12 03:02:28','There will be no restrictions on media in national elections: Information Advisor','Information and Broadcasting Advisor Md. Mahfuz Alam said that there will be no restrictions on the media in this year\'s national parliamentary elections. However, journalists will have to play a cautious, aware and responsible role before, during and after the elections.'),
(556,1,15,NULL,NULL,'Journalist Ruhul Amin Gazi will be a symbol of protest','666565','article','Journalist Ruhul Amin Gazi will be a symbol of protest',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The void left by the late president of Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Journalist leaders said this at a discussion meeting at the Abdus Salam Hall of the National Press Club on Wednesday to mark the first death anniversary of journalist leader Ruhul Amin Gazi. The discussion meeting was organized by the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) and the BNP-backed wing of the Dhaka Union of Journalists (DUJ). The void left by the late president of Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Journalist leaders said this at a discussion meeting at the Abdus Salam Hall of the National Press Club on Wednesday to mark the first death anniversary of journalist leader Ruhul Amin Gazi. The discussion meeting was organized by the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) and the BNP-backed wing of the Dhaka Union of Journalists (DUJ). The void left by the late president of the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Journalist leaders said this at a discussion meeting at the Abdus Salam Hall of the National Press Club on Wednesday to mark the first death anniversary of journalist leader Ruhul Amin Gazi. The discussion meeting was organized by the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) and the BNP-backed wing of the Dhaka Union of Journalists (DUJ). The void left by the late president of the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Journalist leaders made the remarks at a discussion meeting at the Abdus Salam Hall of the National Press Club on Wednesday to mark the first death anniversary of journalist leader Ruhul Amin Gazi. The discussion meeting was organized by the Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) and the BNP-backed wing of the Dhaka Union of Journalists (DUJ).</span></div>','1760086436B6UiV9Hw.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,80,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',31,0,NULL,'2026-03-11 23:32:29','2026-03-11 17:32:29','Journalist Ruhul Amin Gazi will be a symbol of protest','The void left by the late president of Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.The void left by the late president of Bangladesh Federal Union of Journalists (BFUJ) Ruhul Amin Gazi will not be filled. He was one of the protesters against fascism. For this, he had to spend 17 long months in prison. He will remain a symbol of protest.'),
(557,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Prothom Alo wins two categories in the World\'s Best One-Ifra','Prothom-Alo-wins-two-categories-in-the-World\'s-Best-One-Ifra','article',NULL,0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prothom Alo has been recognized as the best in the world in two categories on the global stage of ONE-IFRA. Prothom Alo is the only media outlet in Bangladesh to receive this recognition at the World Printers Summit, the international annual conference of the World Association of News Publishers (ONE-IFRA), the main organization of 3,000 news publishing institutions and entrepreneurs from more than 120 countries.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This year, the main part of this event, the Sustainability and Print Innovation Awards 2025, awards are given in only three categories worldwide. Participating in this global event for the first time, Prothom Alo has won the best award in the highest two categories for the first time.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prothom Alo has received the best award in the ‘Print Advertising Creativity’ category for its diverse creative strategies and initiatives in advertising in regional supplements in different regions of the country throughout the year, and ‘Next Gen Reader Engagement’ for its courageous journalism in the July mass uprising and the involvement of young readers in various initiatives related to this throughout the year. In another category, The Irish Mail of Ireland and New Straits Times of Malaysia jointly won the best award in the ‘Fusion of Print and Digital’ category. Prothom Alo has been recognized as the best in the world in two categories on the global stage of ONE-IFRA. Prothom Alo is the only media outlet from Bangladesh to receive this recognition at the ‘World Printers Summit’, the international annual conference of the World Association of News Publishers (ONE-IFRA), the main organization of 3,000 news publishing institutions and entrepreneurs from more than 120 countries around the world.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The main part of this event, the ‘Sustainability and Print Innovation Awards 2025’, awards were given in only three categories worldwide this year. Prothom Alo participated in this global event for the first time and won the best award in the highest two categories for the first time.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prothom Alo won the best in two categories: \'Print Advertising Creativity\' for its creative advertising strategies and initiatives in regional supplements throughout the year, and \'Next Gen Reader Engagement\' for its courageous journalism during the July Uprising and the involvement of young readers in various initiatives related to this throughout the year. Ireland\'s The Irish Mail and Malaysia\'s New Straits Times jointly won the best in another category, \'Fusion of Print and Digital\'. Prothom Alo has been recognized as the best in the world in two categories on the global stage of ONE-IFRA. Prothom Alo is the only media outlet in Bangladesh to receive this recognition at the \'World Printers Summit\', an international annual conference of the World Association of News Publishers (ONE-IFRA), the main organization of 3,000 news publishing institutions and entrepreneurs from more than 120 countries.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The main part of this event, the Sustainability and Print Innovation Awards 2025, is the only one to be awarded in three categories worldwide this year. Participating in this global event for the first time, Prothom Alo has won the best award in two categories.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Prothom Alo won the best award in the ‘Print Advertising Creativity’ category for its diverse creative strategies and initiatives in advertising in regional supplements in different regions of the country throughout the year, and the ‘Next Gen Reader Engagement’ category for its courageous journalism in the July mass uprising and the involvement of young readers in various initiatives related to this throughout the year. In another category, The Irish Mail of Ireland and New Straits Times of Malaysia jointly won the best award in the ‘Fusion of Print and Digital’ category.</span></div>','1760086700CFdknTMw.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,80,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',40,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 07:48:53','2026-03-07 01:48:53','Prothom Alo wins two categories in the World\'s Best One-Ifra','Prothom Alo has been recognized as the best in the world in two categories on the global stage of ONE-IFRA. Prothom Alo is the only media outlet in Bangladesh to receive this recognition at the World Printers Summit, the international annual conference of the World Association of News Publishers (ONE-IFRA), the main organization of 3,000 news publishing institutions and entrepreneurs from more than 120 countries.'),
(558,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Who wrote the news—human or AI, how does that change credibility?','545454543443','article',NULL,0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">News releases or corporate statements—how credible they are to the reader depends on the identity of the author. If it is said that the text was written by a human, then it seems much more credible to the reader. And if it is said that it was written by artificial intelligence (AI), then the reader\'s trust decreases.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This issue has been raised in a study by the University of Kansas, USA. The research report has been recently published in the international research journal \'Corporate Communications: An International Journal\'. News releases or corporate statements—how credible they are to the reader depends on the identity of the author. If it is said that the text was written by a human, then it seems much more credible to the reader. And if it is said that it was written by artificial intelligence (AI), then the reader\'s trust decreases.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This issue has been raised in a study by the University of Kansas, USA. The research report was recently published in the international research journal ‘Corporate Communications: An International Journal’. Whether a news release or a corporate statement is credible to the reader, it depends on the identity of the author. If it is said that the article was written by a human, then it seems much more credible to the reader. And if it is said that it was written by artificial intelligence (AI), then the reader’s trust decreases.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The issue has been raised in a study by the University of Kansas in the United States. The research report was recently published in the international research journal ‘Corporate Communications: An International Journal’.</span></div>','1760086865sIF3Mxpo.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,80,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',35,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 02:08:44','2026-03-11 20:08:44','Who wrote the news—human or AI, how does that change credibility?','News releases or corporate statements—how credible they are to the reader depends on the identity of the author. If it is said that the text was written by a human, then it seems much more credible to the reader. And if it is said that it was written by artificial intelligence (AI), then the reader\'s trust decreases.'),
(559,1,11,NULL,NULL,'What will be the future of Gaza after the ceasefire, and how many challenges lie ahead?','54454456456564','article','What will be the future of Gaza after the ceasefire, and how many challenges lie ahead?',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Under the constant sound of Israeli drones and warplanes, Jihad Abu Mandil watched his five children play with toy animals in their small makeshift tent in the Deir al-Balah refugee camp in Gaza. It was a glimpse of childhood amid Israel’s ongoing genocide in the besieged territory.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">UN experts and the International Association of Genocide Scholars have recognized the genocide, saying Israel has destroyed almost every source of life in Gaza. It has damaged or destroyed 90 percent of buildings, razing hospitals, universities and entire neighborhoods. Under the constant sound of Israeli drones and warplanes, Jihad Abu Mandil watched his five children play with toy animals in their small makeshift tent in the Deir al-Balah refugee camp in Gaza. It was a glimpse of childhood amid Israel’s ongoing genocide in the besieged territory.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">UN experts and the International Association of Genocide Scholars have acknowledged the genocide, saying Israel has destroyed almost every source of life in Gaza. They have damaged or destroyed 90 percent of buildings, razing hospitals, universities and entire neighborhoods. Under the constant sound of Israeli drones and warplanes, Jihad Abu Mandil watched his five children play with toy animals in their small makeshift tent in the Deir al-Balah refugee camp in Gaza. It was a fleeting glimpse of childhood amid Israel’s ongoing genocide in the besieged territory.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">UN experts and the International Association of Genocide Scholars have acknowledged the genocide, saying Israel has destroyed almost every source of life in Gaza. They have damaged or destroyed 90 percent of the buildings, razing hospitals, universities and entire neighborhoods. Under the constant sound of Israeli drones and warplanes, Jihad Abu Mandil watched his five children play with stuffed animals in their small makeshift tent in the Deir al-Balah refugee camp in Gaza. It was a fleeting glimpse of childhood amid Israel’s ongoing genocide in the besieged territory.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">UN experts and the International Association of Genocide Scholars have recognized this ethnic cleansing, saying that Israel has destroyed almost every source of life in Gaza. They have damaged or destroyed 90 percent of the buildings, razing hospitals, universities and entire neighborhoods.</span></div>','1760086972hzMFQar0.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,75,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',34,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 09:50:17','2026-03-12 03:50:17','What will be the future of Gaza after the ceasefire, and how many challenges lie ahead?','Under the constant sound of Israeli drones and warplanes, Jihad Abu Mandil watched his five children play with toy animals in their small makeshift tent in the Deir al-Balah refugee camp in Gaza. It was a glimpse of childhood amid Israel’s ongoing genocide in the besieged territory.'),
(560,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Israeli cabinet approves Gaza ceasefire deal','54454554','article','Israeli cabinet approves Gaza ceasefire deal',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Israeli government on Friday approved a ceasefire deal with the Palestinian independence group Hamas, paving the way for a ceasefire in Gaza within 24 hours. The process of releasing Israeli hostages could begin within 72 hours.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Israeli cabinet approved the deal this morning, nearly 24 hours after mediators announced a compromise. The deal stipulates that Israel will release Palestinian prisoners in exchange for the release of the hostages. Israel will begin a phased withdrawal of troops from Gaza. The Israeli government on Friday approved a ceasefire deal with the Palestinian independence group Hamas, paving the way for a ceasefire in Gaza within 24 hours. The process of releasing Israeli hostages could begin within 72 hours.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Israeli cabinet approved the deal this morning, nearly 24 hours after mediators announced a compromise. The deal stipulates that Israel will release Palestinian prisoners in exchange for the release of hostages. Israel will begin a phased withdrawal of troops from Gaza. The Israeli government approved a ceasefire deal with the Palestinian independence movement Hamas on Friday, paving the way for a ceasefire in Gaza to take effect within the next 24 hours. The process of releasing Israeli hostages could begin within 72 hours.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Israeli cabinet approved the deal this morning, nearly 24 hours after mediators announced a compromise. The deal stipulates that Israel will release Palestinian prisoners in exchange for the release of hostages. Israel will begin a phased withdrawal of troops from Gaza.</span></div>','1760087084lspfxTsQ.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,75,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',34,0,NULL,'2026-03-12 09:43:35','2026-03-12 03:43:35','Israeli cabinet approves Gaza ceasefire deal','The Israeli government on Friday approved a ceasefire deal with the Palestinian independence group Hamas, paving the way for a ceasefire in Gaza within 24 hours. The process of releasing Israeli hostages could begin within 72 hours.The Israeli government on Friday approved a ceasefire deal with the Palestinian independence group Hamas, paving the way for a ceasefire in Gaza within 24 hours. The process of releasing Israeli hostages could begin within 72 hours.'),
(561,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'A flower garden in the heart of the desert','5544545','article','A flower garden in the heart of the desert',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. The desolate desert, where dust flies most of the year, is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fairy tale in the desert.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Atacama Desert in Chile\'s Llanos de Chayte National Park is filled with wildflowers after unusual rainfall this year. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented rainfall in the mountainous regions and foothills. A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. The desolate desert, where dust flies most of the year, is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fairy tale in the desert.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Atacama Desert in Chile\'s Llanos de Chayte National Park is filled with wildflowers after unusual rainfall this year. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented heavy rain in the mountainous regions and foothills. A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. Where dust flies most of the year, the desolate desert is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fleeting fairy tale in the desert.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Atacama Desert is filled with wildflowers after unusual rainfall this year in Chile\'s Llanos de Chay National Park. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented heavy rain in the mountainous regions and foothills. A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. Where dust flies most of the year, the desolate desert is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fleeting fairy tale in the desert.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Wildflowers have bloomed in Chile\'s Llanos de Chayete National Park after unusually heavy rainfall this year. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented heavy rain in the mountainous regions and foothills. A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. Where dust flies most of the year, the desolate desert is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fleeting fairy tale in the heart of the desert.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Wildflowers have bloomed in Chile\'s Llanos de Chayete National Park after unusually heavy rainfall this year. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented heavy rain in the mountainous regions and foothills.</span></div>','1760087152Xw1uNlFO.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,73,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',41,0,NULL,'2026-03-07 22:21:14','2026-03-07 16:21:14','A flower garden in the heart of the desert','The Atacama Desert in Chile\'s Llanos de Chayte National Park is filled with wildflowers after unusual rainfall this year. The world\'s driest desert receives an average of just two millimeters of rain a year. However, this winter has seen unprecedented rainfall in the mountainous regions and foothills. A rare sight has emerged in Chile\'s Atacama Desert. The desolate desert, where dust flies most of the year, is now covered in a carpet of colorful flowers. It\'s like a fairy tale in the desert.'),
(562,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'US to deploy 200 troops to Gaza','545454545451','article','US to deploy 200 troops to Gaza',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The United States will deploy 200 troops as part of a joint task force in Gaza. However, no separate US troops will be deployed inside Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The United States said that these troops will be deployed to restore stability in Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Two senior US officials confirmed this information on Thursday. Two senior US officials told reporters on condition of anonymity that these 200 troops will be the core of the task force. There will also be representatives from the Egyptian armed forces, Qatar, Turkey and possibly the United Arab Emirates. The United States will deploy 200 troops as part of a joint task force in Gaza. However, no separate US troops will be deployed inside Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The United States said that these troops will be deployed to restore stability in Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Two senior US officials confirmed this information on Thursday. Two senior US officials told reporters on condition of anonymity that these 200 troops will be the core of the task force. There will also be representatives from the Egyptian armed forces, Qatar, Turkey and possibly the United Arab Emirates. The United States will deploy 200 troops as part of a joint task force in Gaza. However, no separate US troops will be deployed inside Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The United States has said that the troops will be deployed to restore stability in Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Two senior US officials confirmed this information on Thursday. Two senior US officials told reporters on condition of anonymity that these 200 troops will be the core of the task force. There will also be representatives from the Egyptian armed forces, Qatar, Turkey and possibly the United Arab Emirates. The United States will deploy 200 troops as part of a joint task force in Gaza. However, no separate US troops will be deployed inside Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The United States has said that these troops will be deployed to restore stability in Gaza.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Two senior US officials confirmed this information on Thursday. Two senior US officials told reporters on condition of anonymity that these 200 troops will be the core of the task force. Representatives from the Egyptian armed forces, Qatar, Türkiye and possibly the United Arab Emirates will also be there.</span></div>','1760087222CtCFZOfB.jpg',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,75,NULL,0,NULL,0,1,0,'true',35,0,NULL,'2026-03-16 02:47:46','2026-03-15 20:47:46','US to deploy 200 troops to Gaza','Two senior US officials confirmed this information on Thursday. Two senior US officials told reporters on condition of anonymity that these 200 troops will be the core of the task force. There will also be representatives from the Egyptian armed forces, Qatar, Turkey and possibly the United Arab Emirates. The United States will deploy 200 troops as part of a joint task force in Gaza. However, no separate US troops will be deployed inside Gaza.'),
(563,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI at OpenAI DevDay in the US','43354345545','article','Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI at OpenAI DevDay in the US',0,1,1,0,1,1,0,NULL,'<div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI has participated in the ‘OpenAI Day 2025’ organized by OpenAI, the maker of ChatGPT. At the conference held in San Francisco, USA, last Monday, OpenAI’s CEO (CEO) Sam Altman and the company’s developer team were met by OneBrain AI officials.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">OneBrain AI announced this in a press release today, Thursday. Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI has participated in the ‘OpenAI Day 2025’ organized by OpenAI, the maker of ChatGPT. At the conference held in San Francisco, USA, last Monday, OpenAI’s CEO (CEO) Sam Altman and the company’s developer team were met by OneBrain AI officials. OneBrain AI announced this in a press release on Thursday. Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI has participated in the ‘OpenAI Day 2025’ organized by OpenAI, the company that makes ChatGPT.</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">OneBrain AI officials met with the company’s developer team, including OpenAI’s CEO Sam Altman, at the conference held in San Francisco, USA, last Monday. OneBrain AI officials met with the company’s developer team, including OpenAI’s CEO Sam Altman, at the conference held in San Francisco, USA last Monday. OneBrain AI officials met with the company’s developer team, including OpenAI’s CEO Sam Altman, at the conference held in San Francisco, USA last Monday. OneBrain AI announced this in a press release on Thursday. Bangladeshi startup OneBrain AI has participated in the \'OpenAI Day 2025\' organized by OpenAI, the maker of ChatGPT. OneBrain AI officials met with the company\'s developer team, including OpenAI\'s CEO Sam Altman, at the conference held in Sa